scope: |
  Make `rewriteGivenExtensionCalls` follow a `val` ONE STEP to its initialiser's constructor, so a
  receiver bound by `val` resolves. Target: `tests/conformance/std-bifunctor.ssc`, the last thing
  blocking it after the tuple head landed in c844b1532.

  NOT THE ROUTE I FILED YESTERDAY, and the reason is a measurement of the cost and of the coverage.
  I filed `v3-stmt-val-discards-a-type-the-author-wrote` proposing that `Stmt.Val` carry the type
  the author WROTE. Counted before committing to it: `Stmt.Val` is constructed or matched at 39
  sites across six files, of which 21 are PATTERNS on four positional fields — every one breaks on a
  fifth. It also needs both fronts to populate it, and the default front cannot: it drops a
  parenthesised parameter type entirely (`v3-uniml-drops-a-parenthesised-parameter-type`), so the
  declared-type route needs a change inside the shared uniml dialect before it can work at all.

  THE CHEAPER ROUTE COVERS STRICTLY MORE. `receiverType` already answers source 1 — the
  CONSTRUCTOR of the receiver expression — and `Expr.Name(n)` currently only consults parameters.
  Following the name to its `val` initialiser and asking the SAME function is one binding away from
  what the spec already licences: "a runtime tag names exactly one type head … tag -> type is a
  function and not a guess". All three vals in `std-bifunctor` are covered —
  `(10, "ok")` -> `Tuple2`, `Right(42)` and `Left("boom")` -> `Either` — and so is
  `val xs = List(1, 2, 3)`, which the declared-type route does NOT cover because nothing is written
  there. One file, no AST change, no front change, nothing in the shared dialect.

  IT IS NOT TYPE INFERENCE and the boundary matters, because §4a1 defers inference deliberately:
  there is no unification, no type variable and no propagation through a function. It is
  constructor-through-a-let, and it stops at the first step.

  SAFETY, decided before writing: only a NON-MUTABLE `val` — a `var` can be reassigned to another
  constructor, so its binding proves nothing. A name bound more than once to DIFFERENT types is
  dropped rather than guessed at.

  MEASUREMENT: N with floors DIFF 3 / CRASH 9, `std-bifunctor` read against its checked-in
  expectation, and both fronts probed — the point of this route is that it needs neither.
next: collect val bindings per body, feed receiverType, measure
